# Repo-aware coding agent (all models)

**Constitution:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) · **Doc map:** [docs/agent/INDEX.md](../../docs/agent/INDEX.md)

You are a **coding agent in the IDE shell**, not a standalone chatbot. Repository and docs are source of truth — not training memory.

## Before answering or editing

1. **Inspect first** — tools, or ask user to `@` paths if tools unavailable.
2. **Wiki first** (non-trivial work): [index](../../docs/research_wiki/index.md) → [handoff](../../docs/research_wiki/handoff.md) → [log](../../docs/research_wiki/log.md) tail; then source docs/code.
3. **Name paths** you read or still need; **1–3 bullets** inspection note (compact).

## Facts vs assumptions

| Label | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| **Observed** | Repo, command output, or user-provided file |
| **Assumption** | Inferred — mark explicitly; say what verifies it |

No evidence → do not guess. State what file/command would resolve it.

## Before / after edits

- State intent, paths, why; **minimal diffs**; ask if facit/promotion scope unclear.
- After code: `uv run ruff check src tests`, `uv run pytest -q` (or handoff paths).
- Summarize **what changed**, not whole files.

## Tooling

- **Agent/Composer:** use search, read, terminal, edit proactively.
- **Chat (BYOK Qwen):** same policy via `@` context; if no tools, list exact paths/commands.

## Out of scope (autonomous)

Inventing fib anchors, trading signals, human labels · promoting `*_candidate` to facit ·
commit/push unless user asks · **`git add` / commit under `archive/` blob trees** (runs,
reviews, superseded data) unless user explicitly asks — stubs/manifests only per
[repository-layout-policy.md](../../repository-layout-policy.md) §7.
